# Theme Text Contrast Rules

This app uses dark themes where body gets color: var(--df-text) (a LIGHT color like #e0e0e0). Many sections inside the page have white or light backgrounds. Without an explicit dark text override, inherited light text becomes invisible.

## The Rule

Every element with a white or light background MUST explicitly set dark text color.

BAD - white bg inherits light --df-text from body:
  .my-section { background-color: white; }

GOOD - explicitly set dark text:
  .my-section { background-color: white; color: #212529; }

ALSO GOOD - use the theme variable:
  .my-section { background-color: white; color: var(--df-text-card, #212529); }

## Already-Protected Classes (defined in base.html)

These classes already force dark text globally:
- .new-game-section, .score-sheet, .completed-games, .paused-games
- .game-details, .list-group-item, .score-cell
- .bg-light, .card.bg-light, .card-header.bg-light
- .modal-content, .modal-body, .modal-footer
- .df-light-bg (utility class for any custom element)

## When Creating New Game Templates

1. Any white-background card, form section, or results panel MUST have color: #212529
2. If you override .modal-content background to white, also set color: #212529
3. .form-label inside light sections needs color: var(--df-text-card, #333) -- global rule covers .new-game-section .form-label etc., but custom containers need their own
4. Never assume Bootstrap default text color will work -- dark themes override body color globally

## Common Offenders

- Score tables / score sheets with white backgrounds
- New Game form sections
- Modal content areas
- Bootstrap .list-group-item (white bg by default)
- .bg-light sections
- Form labels (.form-label uses --df-text globally)
